{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494539-how-do-you-use-animate-lands-gaia-possessed-lands","id":1494539,"title":"How do you use Animate Lands(Gaia-possessed Lands)?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-07T11:29:10-07:00","id":1494539,"title":"How do you use Animate Lands(Gaia-possessed Lands)?","content":"Animate Lands can be found in Possessed, in short they\u2019re land-fomori of Gaia, the whole landscape is given the essence and become a ultimate gaian holy land","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T11:44:01-07:00","id":1494541,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll start with the disclaimer that I\u2019ve never actually used Animate Lands in a game, so this is just theory.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head I think I\u2019d use Animate Lands in probably one of 2-3 ways.<br /> <br /> The first would be if I wanted to underline that \u2018This Land Is Important\u2019 in a WtA chronicle. In this case I\u2019d probably have it be some unspoiled stretch of wilderness, probably with the implication of being a place of highly spiritual importance. The reason for its existence in the narrative would be to exist as a purely sacred and wondrous thing that the Gaians ought to protect with their lives. If they do it makes them seem heroic, if they don\u2019t it makes them seem hopelessly self-defeating, and it makes the agents of any of the Fallen Triat seem villainous for trying to despoil it.<br /> <br /> Another way I might use Animate Lands is to go for a sort of high-animist vibe, where the landscape itself is a character and a social/political entity that must be negotiated with like any other. I\u2019d probably do this for territory of a caern or potential caern and have it be expected that the Garou are going to have to negotiate and work with the Animate Land if they want it\u2019s support. This could be a good way of showing a highly alive world and how all things are related for the garou, including but not limited too the very land itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-08T07:57:23-07:00","id":1494602,"title":"","content":"They could also be a potential alternative to a high-dot Mentor or the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-08T08:14:12-07:00","id":1494604,"title":"","content":"You mean like Kami? Or is this something different?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-08T09:46:38-07:00","id":1494609,"title":"","content":"Animate Lands are a specific type of Kami, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T09:39:12-07:00","id":1494738,"title":"","content":"Yes they are a kind of Kami, the rarest among them (text implies only several are known or survives today). I always think they\u2019re little spiritual kingdom in some ways and can be count as high-dot Caern, they can have rich story ideas","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T10:08:36-07:00","id":1494740,"title":"","content":"I've never actually used an Animate Land in a chronicle, but if I did so, this is how I would do it. First, I would only place it in the most secluded, pristine landscapes possible. While humans may occasionally travel through it or hike there, it would not be a tourist spot and does not have much human infrastructure at all. Only the most serious naturalists would go there. If there are any indigenous people near the land that have long been exposed to it, they purposefully avoid it as a sacred place that is taboo to enter.<br /> <br /> The Animate Land exists to pretty much protect itself with whatever kami powers it has. I would keep this low key so that the impression people would have is that anything that happens is just natural phenomenon. People get lost very easily. Trees or rocks fall to block passages. Wetlands and quicksand swallow up camping gear. Dangerous animals begin to congregate in an area. It's the kind of place that people avoid developing because it is too far away from anything, and it'd be too expensive to pull natural resources from assuming anything could be found there.<br /> <br /> Nearby Garou and other Changing Breeds probably know the Kami exists in some fashion, and do nothing to anger it. They probably leave it alone unless it obviously needs help, or it somehow needs to be informed of some situation. It would be a good place for characters to meditate in, justify XP spend on Gnosis, a place to meet plenty of potential spirit allies, have safe lupus kinfolk, etc.<br /> <br /> As a setting element, it'd be more local flavor than anything else unless the ST wants to run a major plot where PENTEX is trying to &quot;look for oil&quot; or some other pretext to go in and destroy or corrupt the Kami which will take up much of the chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}